# Meet rag-pipeline-utils: RAG for Node.js that tells you when your LLM is making things up 

Your RAG chatbot just told an employee they get thirty vacation days. The handbook it retrieved says twenty. Nothing crashed, no test failed, and the answer reads perfectly well. That's how retrieval-augmented generation usually breaks: quietly.

I maintain `@devilsdev/rag-pipeline-utils`, an open-source RAG library for Node.js built around one idea: you should be able to check every answer against the sources it came from, cheaply, in your app and in CI. This post is a quick tour. 

```
npm install @devilsdev/rag-pipeline-utils

```

Node.js 22+, with CommonJS, ESM and TypeScript types included.

## Catch the made-up sentence 

You don't have to build your pipeline with this library to use it. Bring an answer from anywhere (LangChain, Mastra, the Vercel AI SDK, LlamaIndex or your own code) and pass it in with the sources it was given: 

